  "reason": "Evidence: config_028 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved the best performance (acc=0.678, F1=0.646), showing that multiprofile with avgpool aggregation provides a ~14-point boost over singleprofile. However, we have only tested avgpool aggregation in the multiprofile setting; the effect of transformer aggregation remains untested. Question: config_045 is identical to config_028 except aggregation changes from avgpool to transformer (all other settings: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, weighted). This isolates the effect of aggregation strategy in the most promising configuration family. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable comparison against our current best, directly testing whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) can further improve over simple avgpool. Given the limited budget, confirming or ruling out transformer aggregation in the top-performing setup is the highest-information experiment before exploring other dimensions (image encoder, fusion, RNA encoder variants)."
